// vLLM v1 (ref/vllm at 0c87a197, `vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py`,
// `kv_cache_manager.py`, `block_pool.py`): the two rules a program states
// as expressions, `use "…/lib/vllm.sq";`. docs/language.md §7 has the
// line-by-line correspondence, for `examples/replay/vllm_replay.sq`.

// What a cache hit may cover of a request of x tokens: its full blocks of
// `bs` tokens, and never the last token, which is computed for its logits
// (kv_cache_manager.py:289-300).
def reusable(x, bs) { floor((x - 1) / bs) * bs }

// `long_prefill_token_threshold` as a step stage's `chunk`: the cap `c`
// holds only while more than one request is running or waiting for a slot
// of `reqs`; a request alone takes the whole budget (scheduler.py:606-616).
// `queued(reqs)` counts the waiting holds that name `reqs` first, as a hold
// waits in its first pool's queue; one that names `kv` first is not
// counted. vLLM's count also has `skipped_waiting`,
// which these programs leave empty, and its adaptive threshold (off by
// default) is not modelled.
def long_prefill(reqs, c) { residents + queued(reqs) > 1 ? c : 0 }
